# Supercronic crontab.
#
# No active schedule: every schedule below is commented out. Nothing runs until
# an operator uncomments exactly one line, rebuilds the image, and redeploys.
#
# Format: one line per schedule.
#   <five cron fields>  /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh [-t <name>] "<prompt>"
#
# -t names a destination in NOTIFY_TARGETS. The name must exist there; an
# unknown name fails before sending. A target with a host_scope also tells the
# agent which host the message may talk about, and allow_content false blocks
# the content-search tool for that run. Omit -t to use NOTIFY_DEFAULT_TARGET,
# or the legacy COMPOSIO_ARGS configuration when no default is set.
#
# The five fields are minute, hour, day-of-month, month, day-of-week.
# Times use the container's TZ (set TZ in stack.env; default is UTC).
# Only edit this file and rebuild the image: it is baked in read-only at /app.
# Schedules are trusted operator configuration, not user input.
#
# Examples (uncomment one line per schedule):
#
# Daily digest at 09:00.
# 0 9 * * * /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh "Compose a short daily digest for the team. Use the heading 'Daily digest', list the standing items: review the board, check overnight alerts, and note any blockers. End with a reminder to update the board. Do not invent news or metrics. Send it now with notify.sh."
#
# Morning host + SSH digest at 09:00, to the automations target. This keeps the
# old host-report shape and adds SSH status. The target's host_scope must
# include rossmoney.me, photos.rossmoney.me and vortexservers.co.uk.
# 0 9 * * * /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh -t automations "Compose the morning digest. Call oracle_query first for the 24-hour host statistics, then ssh_probe for SSH status. Use the old host report shape: one line per host with sample count, last-seen age, CPU average and peak, memory average, load average and peak, and disk from the latest sample, plus SSH success with latency or the classified failure. Include every known host in this run, in order. Flag stale hosts (no sample in 20 minutes) and CPU peak >= 90, memory average >= 90, load peak >= 8, disk >= 90. Keep it under 2,000 characters; drop whole host lines from the end and say how many were not shown. Never mention a host outside this run's scope. If SSH is not configured, say so once. Send it now with notify.sh."
#
# Morning Vortex-only digest at 09:00, to the Vortex admin-chat target. The
# target's host_scope must be vortexservers.co.uk only.
# 0 9 * * * /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh -t admin-chat "Compose the morning Vortex digest. Call oracle_query first for the 24-hour host statistics, then ssh_probe for SSH status, for the Vortex hosts only. Use the old host report shape: one line per host with sample count, last-seen age, CPU average and peak, memory average, load average and peak, and disk from the latest sample, plus SSH success with latency or the classified failure. Include every known host in this run, in order. Flag stale hosts (no sample in 20 minutes) and the thresholds. Keep it under 2,000 characters; drop whole host lines from the end and say how many were not shown. Never mention a rossmoney host or anything about it. If SSH is not configured, say so once. Send it now with notify.sh."
#
# Weekdays at 17:30 - end-of-day wrap-up, explicitly to the "general" target.
# 30 17 * * 1-5 /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh -t general "Compose a brief end-of-day wrap-up asking the team to close out their tasks and flag anything that needs attention tomorrow. Send it now with notify.sh."
#
# Every Monday at 08:30 - weekly planning reminder.
# 30 8 * * 1 /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh "Compose a short Monday planning reminder: pick the top three priorities for the week and post them in the channel. Keep it under 300 characters. Send it now with notify.sh."
#
# First day of each month at 10:00 - monthly maintenance note.
# 0 10 1 * * /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh "Compose a short monthly maintenance reminder to rotate credentials and review notification schedules. Send it now with notify.sh."
#
# Every hour at minute 5 - heartbeat (noisy; useful only while testing).
# 5 * * * * /app/scripts/run-prompt.sh "Compose a one-line heartbeat message saying the notification agent is running. Send it now with notify.sh."
